# Python virtual environment
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node modules (once frontend phase starts) — regenerated via npm install
node_modules/

# OS/editor junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
*.swp

# Training checkpoints — only the FINAL model that powers the demo should
# be tracked, not every intermediate save. Ignore the folder by default...
training/checkpoints/*
# ...then explicitly un-ignore the specific final checkpoint file(s) once
# training completes, e.g.:
# !training/checkpoints/final_model.zip

# DELIBERATE NARROW EXCEPTION — evidentiary sweep RESULTS, not model weights.
# The rule above was written about checkpoint .zip files (large, regenerable
# by re-running training). _sweeps/*.json is the opposite: small, and NOT
# regenerable without re-spending the compute that produced it. These files
# are the cited evidence behind claims in CLAUDE.md and BUILD_LOG.md, so
# losing them silently invalidates the record.
#
# Needs THREE lines, not a single `!.../_sweeps/*.json`. Git will not
# re-include a file if one of its parent DIRECTORIES is excluded, and
# `training/checkpoints/*` above excludes the `_sweeps` directory itself —
# so the directory must be un-ignored first, then its contents re-excluded,
# then the .json re-included. Verified: .json tracked, .txt logs still
# ignored, stage*/ checkpoint .zip files still ignored.
!training/checkpoints/_sweeps/
training/checkpoints/_sweeps/*
!training/checkpoints/_sweeps/*.json
# Tier 1 SUMO-activity beacon (sim/sumo_activity.py) — per-machine runtime
# state announcing which process currently drives SUMO. Never committed.
.sumo_active.json
